// A patch for trying live edits (harp play examples/live_demo.harp, after copying it somewhere: cp examples/live_demo.harp ~/live.harp).
// It is made so that a restart or a cut tail is easy to hear: a drone whose filter is swept by a very slow lfo (a full sweep takes 14 s: if a
// save restarted it, you would hear it jump back to the start), a slow arpeggio, and a long reverb.
//
// Things to change while it plays, and what you should hear:
//   the numbers of `cutoff` below           the drone gets brighter or darker; the sweep goes on from where it is
//   `lfo(0.07)` -> `lfo(0.2)`               the sweep gets faster, from where it is (no jump)
//   the notes of `phrase`                   the arpeggio takes the new notes from its next note, in time
//   `bright` list                           the notes get another brightness from the next note; the phrase goes on
//   `decay: 5` of the reverb                the reverb is new (its tail is cut); everything else goes on
//   `gain(0.06)` of the drone               the drone gets louder or quieter; nothing restarts
//   `bpm = 90` -> `bpm = 110`               the arpeggio gets faster at the next step
//   `euclid(16, 9)`                         a new rhythm: the arpeggio starts again; the drone and the reverb go on
//   delete the drone line from `mix`        the drone goes; the reverb tail of it rings out

bpm = 90
steps = 4
seed = 7

// the drone: three saws a few cents apart, an octave and a fifth, through a lowpass that a very slow lfo sweeps
drone = saw([110.0, 110.4, 165.0, 165.6, 220.0]).mix()
cutoff = lfo(0.07).range(300, 2400)
droned = drone.lowPass(cutoff: cutoff, res: 0.35).gain(0.06)

// the arpeggio: a note every two steps, a phrase in A minor that moves a little now and then
phrase = degrees(a3, minor, mutate([0 2 4 7 4 2 0 -3], swap: 0.3))
bright = [1800 2800 2200 3400 6700]

fn pluck(gate, note, cutoff) {
  f = hz(note)
  tone = saw([f * 0.997, f * 1.003])
  body = tone.lowPass(cutoff: cutoff * (0.4 + 0.6 * env(gate, [0 1 0], [0.003 0.4], -4)), res: 0.25)
  body * env(gate, [0 1 0], [0.003 0.5], -4) * 0.22
}

arp = play(pluck, rhythm: euclid(15, 8), legato: 0.5, fields: [phrase, bright], voices: 3)

// the echo of the arpeggio, and everything through a long reverb
echoed = arp.echo(max: 1, time: [0.5, 0.75], feedback: 0.4, mix: 0.3)

mix = droned.dup() + echoed

out = mix.reverb(mix: 0.3, decay: 5)
